WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.508 --> 00:00:02.110
(upbeat)

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.004
- [Narrator] This is the collared aracari,

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.483
a toucan native to the
tropical rainforests

00:00:07.483 --> 00:00:09.850
in Central and South America.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:12.337
Their bodies are a
gorgeous rainbow of colors

00:00:12.337 --> 00:00:16.315
with bright plumage and
large colorful bills.

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:19.040
Their bills are the most distinct feature.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.825
The upper part has a saw tooth pattern,

00:00:21.825 --> 00:00:25.785
helping them reach food on
branches they can't land on.

00:00:25.785 --> 00:00:29.017
Collared aracaris reach
just over a foot long

00:00:29.017 --> 00:00:31.743
and weigh up to 10 ounces.

00:00:31.743 --> 00:00:34.333
Most of that size comes from their bills,

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:38.180
they take up over a
quarter of its entire body.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.465
They mainly eat fruit,

00:00:39.465 --> 00:00:42.681
but occasionally feed on small insects.

00:00:42.681 --> 00:00:45.176
While they are found in
abundance throughout their range,

00:00:45.176 --> 00:00:47.827
their population has been decreasing

00:00:47.827 --> 00:00:50.421
due to a combination of deforestation

00:00:50.421 --> 00:00:53.325
and hunting for the pet trade.

00:00:53.325 --> 00:00:55.825
This is the collared aracari.

